From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu_umd: DirectX 12 Ultimate (feature level 12_2), MSAA

The D3D12 DDI's DirectX 12 Ultimate features, passed on to vkd3d-proton:

- Variable rate shading: RSSetShadingRate and RSSetShadingRateImage (tier 2
  caps from vkd3d-proton).
- Mesh and amplification shaders: CreateMeshShader/CreateAmplificationShader
  (containers with the mesh shader's vertex and primitive output signatures,
  OSG1/PSG1), mesh pipelines as pipeline state streams, DispatchMesh.
- Ray tracing (umd_raytracing.cpp): state objects (collections, ray tracing
  pipelines, AddToStateObject), whose subobjects are the API's but for the
  associations: the runtime resolves those into an export summary, passed on
  as an explicit association per export and associated subobject; DXIL
  libraries get a container. Shader identifiers and stack sizes,
  acceleration structure prebuild info, builds, copies and postbuild info,
  SetPipelineState1, DispatchRays. Tier from vkd3d-proton (1.1).
- Sampler feedback: feedback maps (DESC1 with their mip region, through
  ID3D12Device8), CreateSamplerFeedbackUnorderedAccessView, the tier (0.9).
- Feature level 12_2 when vkd3d-proton has it.

Found on the way:
- MSAA: CheckMultisampleQualityLevels answered 0 for every sample count above
  1, so no multisampled render target could be made at all. It now has
  vkd3d-proton's levels, and format support its multisample render target
  and load bits: the runtime refuses the device unless every typed format's
  levels agree with its multisample render target bit, so formats that only
  view multisampled ones (R32_FLOAT_X8X24_TYPELESS...) get none; typeless
  formats keep their family's.
- WriteBufferImmediate was there but reported unsupported: its queue flags
  are vkd3d-proton's now (12_2 wants them).

12_2 also needs 40 bits of GPU virtual address a process: the viogpu3d kernel
driver's page tables (kvm-guest-drivers-windows 0021).
